From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 13 Sep 2026 10:43:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/4] media: apple: avd: allocate the job segment table with
 kvcalloc

The job segment table holds one struct avd_segment of 2056 bytes per
slice, plus the header. In 7.1 avd_init_job() allocated MAX_SLICES (4096)
of them, about 8.4 MB, with kzalloc() for every frame; once the page cache
was full of file pages (an NVR writing recordings) that order-10
allocation failed, the frame came back with an error and the output
silently lost frames (four concurrent 2304x1296 decodes on T6000).

7.2 sizes the table by the expected slice count (one per macroblock row,
plus one) and grows it by half when a frame has more slices, so a
1296-line stream needs about 170 KB: still a physically contiguous
order-4 allocation on a 16K-page kernel, for every frame, and more
while it grows.

The table is only read by the CPU (its instructions are written to MMIO
with writel()), so it does not need physically contiguous memory. Use
kvcalloc()/kvfree() for it everywhere: avd_init_job(), avd_submit_job(),
and the H.264 grow and error paths. kvcalloc() also checks the
multiplication for overflow.

Signed-off-by: aquarat <3090997+aquarat@users.noreply.github.com>
[7.2.11 port: also the H.264 grow path (avd_h264_realloc_slices) and its
 error path, which 7.2 added.]
---
 avd-drv.c  | 4 ++--
 avd-h264.c | 8 ++++----
 2 files changed, 6 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/avd-drv.c b/avd-drv.c
index 5f0e4a0..4c7bfb9 100644
--- a/avd-drv.c
+++ b/avd-drv.c
@@ -139,7 +139,7 @@ int avd_init_job(struct avd_ctx *ctx, enum avd_codec codec, size_t segments)
 
 	job->codec = codec;
 	job->num = 0;
-	job->segments = kzalloc(sizeof(*job->segments) * segments, GFP_KERNEL);
+	job->segments = kvcalloc(segments, sizeof(*job->segments), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!job->segments)
 		ret = -ENOMEM;
 	return ret;
@@ -187,7 +187,7 @@ int avd_submit_job(struct avd_ctx *ctx)
 		       reg);
 	}
 
-	kfree(sub->segments);
+	kvfree(sub->segments);
 	sub->segments = NULL;
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/avd-h264.c b/avd-h264.c
index ef81356..edb5280 100644
--- a/avd-h264.c
+++ b/avd-h264.c
@@ -748,8 +748,8 @@ static int avd_h264_realloc_slices(struct avd_ctx *ctx)
 	kfree(tmp);
 
 	tmp = ctx->job.segments;
-	ctx->job.segments = kzalloc(
-		sizeof(*ctx->job.segments) * (alloc_slice_num + 1), GFP_KERNEL);
+	ctx->job.segments = kvcalloc(alloc_slice_num + 1,
+				     sizeof(*ctx->job.segments), GFP_KERNEL);
 	if (!ctx->job.segments) {
 		ctx->job.segments = tmp;
 		return -ENOMEM;
@@ -757,7 +757,7 @@ static int avd_h264_realloc_slices(struct avd_ctx *ctx)
 
 	memcpy(ctx->job.segments, tmp,
 	       sizeof(*ctx->job.segments) * (ctx->job.num + 1));
-	kfree(tmp);
+	kvfree(tmp);
 
 	return 0;
 }
@@ -829,7 +829,7 @@ static int avd_h264_run(struct avd_ctx *ctx)
 	return avd_submit_job(ctx);
 
 err_free_jobs:
-	kfree(ctx->job.segments);
+	kvfree(ctx->job.segments);
 	return ret;
 }
 
